###############################################################################
# Set default behavior to automatically normalize line endings.
###############################################################################
* text=auto

###############################################################################
# The files something takes a SHA-256 of, and what keeps that hash honest.
#
# `* text=auto` above stores every text file as LF and then hands the working
# tree whatever the platform asks for -- CRLF on Windows. That is right for
# source a compiler reads and wrong for a file something HASHES, because the
# hash then describes a checkout rather than the content.
#
# Build/BakeFont.py is such a file: it records its own sha256 in the header it
# bakes (ADR-073), and Build/CheckProjectFiles.py re-derives that from disk. On
# 2026-09-13 main went red on exactly this -- the header carried the LF hash
# ec81843f, the Windows runner checked the baker out as CRLF, and the identical
# file hashed 75fae9ab. Re-baking cannot settle it: the two machines disagree
# about the line endings, not about the font.
#
# `eol=lf` invents no convention. .editorconfig has declared LF for *.py all
# along, and the bake was taken on a machine that honoured it; this is what
# makes git hand over the file .editorconfig already says is there.
#
# The TTFs are left alone today because git reads a NUL byte in their first
# 8 KiB and calls them binary. That is a heuristic, and a hashed source should
# not rest on one, so it is stated. Content is unchanged either way.
###############################################################################
*.py  text eol=lf
*.ttf binary

###############################################################################
# The resource files, for the reason the TTFs are named above.
#
# `LockStep.ico` is byte-exact in a way nothing checks: its 118-byte directory
# declares the size and depth of each of the seven images behind it, and Windows
# picks which image to draw by reading THAT and not the images (ADR-111's
# activation commit; `LoadImage` defers to `LookupIconIdFromDirectoryEx`). A
# directory that has been edited is a blurry taskbar icon and nothing louder --
# no error, no failed build.
#
# `Lockstep.rc` is UTF-16LE, which is what the Visual Studio resource editor
# writes. A line-ending normalisation inside UTF-16 does not correct a file, it
# destroys one: the bytes CR and LF are half of a code unit there.
#
# Both are left alone today only because git finds a NUL byte in the first 8 KiB
# and calls them binary. That is a heuristic, and neither of these should rest on
# one, so it is stated -- the same argument, and the same remedy, as the TTFs.
###############################################################################
*.ico binary
*.rc  binary

###############################################################################
# Set default behavior for command prompt diff.
#
# This is need for earlier builds of msysgit that does not have it on by
# default for csharp files.
# Note: This is only used by command line
###############################################################################
#*.cs     diff=csharp

###############################################################################
# Set the merge driver for project and solution files
#
# Merging from the command prompt will add diff markers to the files if there
# are conflicts (Merging from VS is not affected by the settings below, in VS
# the diff markers are never inserted). Diff markers may cause the following 
# file extensions to fail to load in VS. An alternative would be to treat
# these files as binary and thus will always conflict and require user
# intervention with every merge. To do so, just uncomment the entries below
###############################################################################
#*.sln       merge=binary
#*.csproj    merge=binary
#*.vbproj    merge=binary
#*.vcxproj   merge=binary
#*.vcproj    merge=binary
#*.dbproj    merge=binary
#*.fsproj    merge=binary
#*.lsproj    merge=binary
#*.wixproj   merge=binary
#*.modelproj merge=binary
#*.sqlproj   merge=binary
#*.wwaproj   merge=binary

###############################################################################
# behavior for image files
#
# image files are treated as binary by default.
###############################################################################
#*.jpg   binary
#*.png   binary
#*.gif   binary

###############################################################################
# diff behavior for common document formats
# 
# Convert binary document formats to text before diffing them. This feature
# is only available from the command line. Turn it on by uncommenting the 
# entries below.
###############################################################################
#*.doc   diff=astextplain
#*.DOC   diff=astextplain
#*.docx  diff=astextplain
#*.DOCX  diff=astextplain
#*.dot   diff=astextplain
#*.DOT   diff=astextplain
#*.pdf   diff=astextplain
#*.PDF   diff=astextplain
#*.rtf   diff=astextplain
#*.RTF   diff=astextplain
